        "A surrealist masterpiece comes to eerie life as Leonardo da Vinci's enigmatic Mona Lisa portrait transforms from a serene smile into a terrifying visage. The subject's gaze once cast downward in quiet contemplation now blazes with an otherworldly intensity, as she crawls out of the golden frame and onto the Renaissance-era tableaux. Her features contort, elongating into grotesque, nightmarish proportions, her skin stretching taut over bony facial structure. The American Gothic-inspired details of her attire – the ruffles, the lace – now appear twisted and macabre, like the petals of a dark flower unfolding to reveal its deadly core. As she rises from the canvas, the Mona Lisa's once-subtle smile now twists into a malevolent snarl, illuminating the dark recesses of the room with an unearthly glow."
